        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://fairfieldborough.com/history-events/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "During the Civil War, Union cavalry under Major Samuel Starr fought Virginia cavalry near Fairfield, and the town hosted wounded soldiers in private homes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairfield%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Fairfield sits on the historic Confederate retreat route, where General Robert E. Lee's army passed through the town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitpa.com/explore/regions/dutch-country-roads/fairfield/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Fairfield Historic District and Fairfield Inn are listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairfield%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The abandoned 'tapeworm railroad' of Thaddeus Stevens would have stopped in Fairfield if not abandoned in 1838, and its railbed later helped escaped slaves on the Underground Railroad.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        10
      ],
